    "prompt": "The UnrecognizedUnit class\u2019s equality comparison is currently misbehaving when an instance is compared with None or other non-unit types. In scenarios where a unit is unrecognized (for example, created with a non-standard string using parse_strict='silent'), the conversion process fails and leads to a TypeError rather than a simple False result. The fix requires modifying the __eq__ method in the UnrecognizedUnit class so that it properly catches exceptions during the conversion and returns NotImplemented. This update will allow comparisons such as x == None to evaluate safely to False without triggering errors.",
    "hint_texts": "In the UnrecognizedUnit class, locate the __eq__ method (approximately at line 1710 in astropy/units/core.py). Wrap the conversion of 'other' in a try/except block that captures ValueError, UnitsError, and TypeError. In the except clause, return NotImplemented rather than letting the exception propagate. After successful conversion, compare the names of the units ensuring that the types match. This modification will align the behavior of UnrecognizedUnit with the expected comparison logic described in the problem statement.",
